  "title": "Epic of Sundiata (Sun-Jata), Mande oral epic",
  "summary": "The Epic of Sundiata is a West African oral epic about the founder of the Mali empire, performed publicly only by professional bards called griots. Columbia University's epics project dates the oral tradition to the 13th century CE. UNESCO records that the Sosso-Bala balafon, kept in the village of Nyagassola in northern Guinea, has carried the epic down the centuries. This is tradition, not a dated chronicle.",
